From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PeterXMR <xmrpeter@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:15:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: Add Pixel 6a (bluejay)
 first-light board

Add a first-light board file for the Pixel 6a: oriole's board file with
bluejay's model and compatible, without oriole's two board-specific
LDOs. Everything it enables, it enables as oriole's does, through
gs101-pixel-common.dtsi: the console UART, USB, both cluster watchdogs,
UFS and its PHY, the S2MPG10/11 regulators, the MAX77759 Type-C
controller, fuel gauge and PMIC, and the battery EEPROM. The GPU stays
disabled, and there is no panel or touch node.

bluejay boots the same two gs101 base device trees as oriole and raven:
Google's bluejay tree builds every bluejay board overlay on
gs101/gs101-a0.dtb and gs101/gs101-b0.dtb, whose soc_id is 0x09845000
and 0x09845001. So this DTB carries the B0 value as oriole's does, and
the image tooling writes the A0 copy from it.

The panel is a 1080x2400 S6E3FC3 variant (samsung,s6e3fc3_6a in
Google's gs101-bluejay-display.dtsi), oriole's size, so the splash
carve-out and the simple-framebuffer keep oriole's values. The retail
board overlay is MP 1.0, board_id 0x20506 and board_rev 0x10000; the
board dtbo for ABL and the image packing live in the omarchy-mobile
repository (device/bluejay).

Oriole's ldo14m (avdd18_tcxo) and ldo31m (nfc) are left out. Upstream
marks both as board specific, and Google's bluejay tree takes both from
the shared gs101-pmic.dtsi, regulator-always-on there: L14M_AVDD_TCXO,
and L31M, which gs101-whitefin2-pmic.dtsi (included by bluejay and by
oriole) renames to L31M_DISP_VDDI. Left undescribed, they stay as the
bootloader leaves them, as on raven.

Not booted yet: no Pixel 6a has run this tree. Apart from the model,
the compatible, the LDO block and its regulator include, the file
matches oriole's, its comments on soc_id and the bootargs included; the
splash and framebuffer blocks are oriole's text, so its copyright lines
stay. The only other
differences between the two boards in postmarketOS's gs101-bluejay.dts
are ST FTS touch values, for a driver this tree does not have.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/bluejay/+/refs/tags/android-16.0.0_r0.9/dts/gs101-bluejay-mp1_0.dts
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/bluejay/+/refs/tags/android-16.0.0_r0.9/dts/gs101-bluejay-display.dtsi
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/bluejay/+/refs/tags/android-16.0.0_r0.9/dts/Makefile
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/gs101/+/refs/tags/android-16.0.0_r0.9/dts/gs101-b0.dts
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/gs101/+/refs/tags/android-16.0.0_r0.9/dts/gs101-pmic.dtsi
Link: https://gitlab.postmarketos.org/soc/tensor-exynos/linux/-/blob/e8f42849a581/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-bluejay.dts
Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
Signed-off-by: PeterXMR <xmrpeter@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/Makefile    |  2 +
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-bluejay.dts  | 46 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 48 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-bluejay.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/Makefile
index 90969cf84..8e651de7d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/Makefile
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_EXYNOS) += \
+	gs101-bluejay.dtb \
 	gs101-oriole.dtb \
 	gs101-raven.dtb \
 	gs201-cheetah.dtb \
@@ -11,6 +12,7 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_EXYNOS) += \
 	zumapro-tegu.dtb
 
 # ABL applies board overlays, so keep symbols for labels
+DTC_FLAGS_gs101-bluejay += -@
 DTC_FLAGS_gs101-oriole += -@
 DTC_FLAGS_gs101-raven += -@
 DTC_FLAGS_gs201-cheetah += -@
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-bluejay.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-bluejay.dts
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..e74fb3b35
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-bluejay.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * Bluejay Device Tree
+ *
+ * Copyright 2021-2023 Google LLC
+ * Copyright 2023 Linaro Ltd - <peter.griffin@linaro.org>
+ */
+
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include "gs101-pixel-common.dtsi"
+
+/ {
+	model = "Bluejay";
+	compatible = "google,gs101-bluejay", "google,gs101";
+
+	/*
+	 * ABL picks the base DTB by soc_id (product id 0x09845000 | major
+	 * revision); the factory vendor_boot carries one per revision. B0 = 1.
+	 */
+	soc_id = <0x09845001 0x0>;
+
+	chosen {
+		/*
+		 * ABL appends its own arguments (console=null among them), so a
+		 * panic is silent: panic=10 reboots instead of hanging. init hands
+		 * over to the Arch root on userdata when it finds one.
+		 */
+		bootargs = "console=tty0 panic=10 clk_ignore_unused pd_ignore_unused rdinit=/init";
+	};
+};
+
+&cont_splash_mem {
+	reg = <0x0 0xfac00000 (1080 * 2400 * 4)>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&framebuffer0 {
+	width = <1080>;
+	height = <2400>;
+	stride = <(1080 * 4)>;
+	format = "a8r8g8b8";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
